# Product Gallery App — Codebase Summary

A small **Next.js App Router** product gallery. No animation libraries, no View Transitions yet, no real images. Next **16.3.0-canary.80** already ships the APIs needed for the transitions you want (docs included under `node_modules/next/dist/docs`).

---

## 1. Overall project structure

```
/workspace
├── package.json              # next@^16.3.0-canary.80, react@19.1.0
├── next.config.ts            # empty config (viewTransition NOT enabled)
├── tsconfig.json             # path alias @/* → ./*
├── app/
│   ├── layout.tsx            # Root layout, metadata, imports globals.css
│   ├── page.tsx              # Home: Products grid + Suspense
│   ├── ProductGrid.tsx       # Client-facing grid of product cards
│   ├── ProductSkeleton.tsx   # Grid skeleton fallback
│   ├── globals.css           # All styles (plain CSS, no Tailwind)
│   └── product/[slug]/
│       └── page.tsx          # Product detail page
└── lib/
    └── products.ts           # Product type + static data + getProduct()
```

| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Framework** | Next.js App Router (canary 16.3) |
| **React** | 19.1.0 (Next uses its own compiled canary React with `ViewTransition`) |
| **Language** | TypeScript |
| **Routing** | File-based: `/` and `/product/[slug]` |
| **Styling** | Single plain CSS file (`globals.css`) — no Tailwind/CSS modules |
| **Data** | Static in-memory array in `lib/products.ts` |
| **Config** | `next.config.ts` is empty: `const nextConfig: NextConfig = {}` |

### Key files

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `/workspace/app/layout.tsx` | Root layout: `<html>`, `<body>`, metadata |
| `/workspace/app/page.tsx` | Home page with Suspense → ProductGrid |
| `/workspace/app/ProductGrid.tsx` | Renders product cards as `Link`s |
| `/workspace/app/ProductSkeleton.tsx` | 4-card skeleton grid |
| `/workspace/app/product/[slug]/page.tsx` | Detail page + inline DetailsSkeleton + ProductDetails |
| `/workspace/app/globals.css` | Layout, cards, detail, skeletons, pulse keyframe |
| `/workspace/lib/products.ts` | `Product` type, 4 products, `getProduct()` |
| `/workspace/next.config.ts` | Empty — needs `experimental.viewTransition: true` |

No `components/` folder, no middleware, no loading.tsx files, no template.tsx, no client components (`'use client'` nowhere).

---

## 2. Product grid and product detail pages

### Data model (`/workspace/lib/products.ts`)

```ts
export type Product = {
  slug: string
  name: string
  description: string
  price: number
  color: string  // used as backgroundColor stand-in for images
}

export const products: Product[] = [
  { slug: 'classic-sneakers', name: 'Classic Sneakers', ..., color: '#4F46E5' },
  { slug: 'leather-backpack', ... color: '#059669' },
  { slug: 'wireless-headphones', ... color: '#DC2626' },
  { slug: 'cotton-hoodie', ... color: '#D97706' },
]

export function getProduct(slug: string): Product | undefined
```

### Grid (`ProductGrid` → home page)

```tsx
// app/ProductGrid.tsx
export function ProductGrid() {
  return (
    <div className="product-grid">
      {products.map((product) => (
        <Link key={product.slug} href={`/product/${product.slug}`} className="product-card">
          <div className="product-image" style={{ backgroundColor: product.color }} />
          <h2>{product.name}</h2>
          <p>${product.price}</p>
        </Link>
      ))}
    </div>
  )
}
```

- **Not async** — data is sync; Suspense on home is mainly structural (skeleton always available).
- Image = colored `div.product-image` (aspect-ratio 4/3), not `<img>` or `next/image`.

### Detail (`app/product/[slug]/page.tsx`)

```tsx
export default async function ProductPage({
  params,
}: { params: Promise<{ slug: string }> }) {
  const { slug } = await params
  const product = products.find((p) => p.slug === slug)
  if (!product) notFound()

  return (
    <div>
      <Link href="/" className="back-link">← Back to products</Link>
      <div className="product-detail">
        <div className="product-hero" style={{ backgroundColor: product.color }} />
        <Suspense fallback={<DetailsSkeleton />}>
          <ProductDetails slug={slug} />
        </Suspense>
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}
```

- **Hero image** is sync (same color div), outside Suspense.
- **Text** (`ProductDetails`) is async with artificial `100ms` delay:

```tsx
async function ProductDetails({ slug }: { slug: string }) {
  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 100))
  const product = getProduct(slug)
  if (!product) notFound()
  return (
    <div className="product-info">
      <h1>{product.name}</h1>
      <p className="product-price">${product.price}</p>
      <p className="product-description">{product.description}</p>
    </div>
  )
}
```

- Params use Next 15+ style: `params: Promise<{ slug: string }>`.
- Layout: CSS grid 2 columns (`.product-detail`), hero + info.

---

## 3. Navigation between pages

| From | To | Mechanism |
|------|-----|-----------|
| Grid card | `/product/[slug]` | `next/link` `<Link href={...}>` wrapping card |
| Detail | `/` | `<Link href="/" className="back-link">` |

No `useRouter`, no `router.push`, no `transitionTypes`, no shared layout chrome beyond root layout.

```tsx
// Grid → detail
<Link href={`/product/${product.slug}`} className="product-card">...</Link>

// Detail → home
<Link href="/" className="back-link">← Back to products</Link>
```

---

## 4. Existing animation / transition code

**Almost none.** Only skeleton pulse:

```css
/* globals.css */
.skeleton-image { background: #e5e5e5; animation: pulse 1.5s ease-in-out infinite; }
.skeleton-text  { ... animation: pulse 1.5s ease-in-out infinite; }

@keyframes pulse {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  50%      { opacity: 0.5; }
}
```

No:
- CSS page transitions
- Framer Motion / Motion
- `view-transition-name`
- `::view-transition-*` rules
- `prefers-reduced-motion`
- React `<ViewTransition>`
- `experimental.viewTransition` in config

---

## 5. Image components for products

**There are no real images.** Products use solid-color divs:

| Location | Class | Aspect | Content |
|----------|-------|--------|---------|
| Grid thumbnail | `.product-image` | 4 / 3 | `backgroundColor: product.color` |
| Detail hero | `.product-hero` | 1 / 1 | `backgroundColor: product.color` |

No `next/image`, no `<img>`, no external URLs. Shared-element morph targets should wrap these two divs with matching `ViewTransition` `name`s (e.g. `product-${slug}`).

---

## 6. Loading / Suspense / skeletons

### Home (`app/page.tsx`)

```tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react'
import { ProductGrid } from './ProductGrid'
import { ProductGridSkeleton } from './ProductSkeleton'

export default function Home() {
  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Products</h1>
      <Suspense fallback={<ProductGridSkeleton />}>
        <ProductGrid />
      </Suspense>
    </main>
  )
}
```

`ProductGridSkeleton` (`ProductSkeleton.tsx`): 4 cards with `.skeleton-image` + two `.skeleton-text` bars.

### Detail (`product/[slug]/page.tsx`)

- Inline `DetailsSkeleton` (large + short + normal skeleton text).
- Hero is **not** skeletoned (renders immediately).
- No `loading.tsx` route segment files.
- No shared skeleton → content transition (instant Suspense swap).

---

## 7. CSS / styling approach

- **Plain global CSS** only (`app/globals.css`, imported in layout).
- System font stack, light gray background `#fafafa`.
- Utility-ish class names: `.product-grid`, `.product-card`, `.product-image`, `.product-detail`, `.product-hero`, `.product-info`, `.product-price`, `.product-description`, `.back-link`, skeleton classes.
- No CSS modules, Tailwind, styled-components, or CSS-in-JS.
- Reset: universal `margin/padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box`.
- Grid: `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(250px, 1fr))`, gap `1.5rem`.
- Cards: white bg, 12px radius, light shadow, `text-decoration: none`.

All new view-transition CSS should go in `globals.css` (matching the official guide).

---

## 8. `package.json` dependencies

```json
{
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "next dev",
    "build": "next build",
    "start": "next start"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "next": "^16.3.0-canary.80",
    "react": "19.1.0",
    "react-dom": "19.1.0"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@types/node": "^20",
    "@types/react": "^19",
    "@types/react-dom": "^19",
    "@vitejs/plugin-react": "^4.4.1",
    "typescript": "^5",
    "vite-tsconfig-paths": "^5.1.4",
    "vitest": "^3.1.3"
  }
}
```

- **No** framer-motion, motion, GSAP, or other animation libs.
- Vitest present but no app tests under the app tree.
- Path alias `@/*` → project root.

---

## 9. View Transitions API / related libraries

| Status | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| **App usage** | Not used anywhere in app code |
| **Config** | `experimental.viewTransition` **not** set |
| **Libraries** | None installed for VT |
| **Next docs** | Full guide at `node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/view-transitions.md` |
| **Config API** | `node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/viewTransition.md` |
| **Link API** | `transitionTypes` prop documented (added v16.2.0) |
| **Runtime** | Next’s compiled React **exports** `ViewTransition` (`next/dist/compiled/react/...`) |
| **Top-level `react` package** | 19.1.0 does **not** export `ViewTransition` itself; App Router uses Next’s canary React when the flag is on |

Official demo referenced in docs:  
https://react-view-transitions-demo.labs.vercel.dev  
https://github.com/vercel-labs/react-view-transitions-demo

---

## Implementation map (what to touch for your four goals)

This app is essentially the “before” state of the official Next view-transitions guide (gallery thumbnail → detail, Suspense reveal, directional nav, reduced motion).

### A. Enable the feature

```ts
// next.config.ts
import type { NextConfig } from 'next'

const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  experimental: {
    viewTransition: true,
  },
}

export default nextConfig
```

```tsx
import { ViewTransition } from 'react'  // via Next's React canary when flag is on
```

### B. Shared element: grid thumbnail → detail hero

**Files:** `ProductGrid.tsx`, `product/[slug]/page.tsx`, `globals.css`

```tsx
// ProductGrid.tsx — wrap thumbnail
import { ViewTransition } from 'react'

<Link
  key={product.slug}
  href={`/product/${product.slug}`}
  className="product-card"
  transitionTypes={['nav-forward']}  // also for directional slides
>
  <ViewTransition name={`product-${product.slug}`} share="morph">
    <div className="product-image" style={{ backgroundColor: product.color }} />
  </ViewTransition>
  <h2>{product.name}</h2>
  <p>${product.price}</p>
</Link>
```

```tsx
// product/[slug]/page.tsx — wrap hero with SAME name
<ViewTransition name={`product-${product.slug}`} share="morph">
  <div className="product-hero" style={{ backgroundColor: product.color }} />
</ViewTransition>
```

```css
/* optional morph polish */
::view-transition-group(.morph) { animation-duration: 400ms; }
::view-transition-image-pair(.morph) { animation-name: via-blur; }
@keyframes via-blur {
  30% { filter: blur(3px); }
}
```

**Important:** Matching `name` is the identity key. Hero and thumbnail must share `product-${slug}`.

### C. Directional page navigation slides

**Files:** both Link sites + wrap page content + CSS

```tsx
// Forward (grid → detail)
<Link href={...} transitionTypes={['nav-forward']}>

// Back (detail → home)
<Link href="/" className="back-link" transitionTypes={['nav-back']}>
```

```tsx
// Wrap page content (home main and/or detail content)
<ViewTransition
  enter={{ 'nav-forward': 'nav-forward', 'nav-back': 'nav-back', default: 'none' }}
  exit={{ 'nav-forward': 'nav-forward', 'nav-back': 'nav-back', default: 'none' }}
  default="none"
>
  {/* page content */}
</ViewTransition>
```

```css
::view-transition-old(.nav-forward) {
  --slide-offset: -60px;
  animation: 150ms ease-in both fade reverse, 400ms ease-in-out both slide reverse;
}
::view-transition-new(.nav-forward) {
  --slide-offset: 60px;
  animation: 210ms ease-out 150ms both fade, 400ms ease-in-out both slide;
}
::view-transition-old(.nav-back) {
  --slide-offset: 60px;
  animation: 150ms ease-in both fade reverse, 400ms ease-in-out both slide reverse;
}
::view-transition-new(.nav-back) {
  --slide-offset: -60px;
  animation: 210ms ease-out 150ms both fade, 400ms ease-in-out both slide;
}
@keyframes slide {
  from { translate: var(--slide-offset); }
  to   { translate: 0; }
}
@keyframes fade {
  from { filter: blur(3px); opacity: 0; }
  to   { filter: blur(0); opacity: 1; }
}
```

Note: browser back/gesture won’t get `transitionTypes`; shared morph still works if names match.

### D. Smooth Suspense skeleton → content

**Files:** `page.tsx` (grid), `product/[slug]/page.tsx` (details), `globals.css`

```tsx
// Detail text handoff (already has 100ms delay → Suspense will show)
import { Suspense, ViewTransition } from 'react'

<Suspense
  fallback={
    <ViewTransition exit="slide-down">
      <DetailsSkeleton />
    </ViewTransition>
  }
>
  <ViewTransition enter="slide-up" default="none">
    <ProductDetails slug={slug} />
  </ViewTransition>
</Suspense>
```

Same pattern for home grid if you make `ProductGrid` async (or keep structure ready):

```tsx
// app/page.tsx
<Suspense
  fallback={
    <ViewTransition exit="slide-down">
      <ProductGridSkeleton />
    </ViewTransition>
  }
>
  <ViewTransition enter="slide-up" default="none">
    <ProductGrid />
  </ViewTransition>
</Suspense>
```

```css
:root {
  --duration-exit: 150ms;
  --duration-enter: 210ms;
}
::view-transition-old(.slide-down) {
  animation:
    var(--duration-exit) ease-out both fade reverse,
    var(--duration-exit) ease-out both slide-y reverse;
}
::view-transition-new(.slide-up) {
  animation:
    var(--duration-enter) ease-in var(--duration-exit) both fade,
    400ms ease-in both slide-y;
}
@keyframes slide-y {
  from { transform: translateY(10px); }
  to   { transform: translateY(0); }
}
```

`default="none"` on enter content avoids fighting the shared morph / nav slides.

### E. `prefers-reduced-motion`

```css
/* globals.css */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  ::view-transition-old(*),
  ::view-transition-new(*),
  ::view-transition-group(*) {
    animation-duration: 0s !important;
    animation-delay: 0s !important;
  }

  /* also stop skeleton pulse */
  .skeleton-image,
  .skeleton-text {
    animation: none;
  }
}
```

---

## File checklist for implementation

| File | Changes needed |
|------|----------------|
| `/workspace/next.config.ts` | `experimental.viewTransition: true` |
| `/workspace/app/ProductGrid.tsx` | `ViewTransition` on image; `transitionTypes` on Link |
| `/workspace/app/product/[slug]/page.tsx` | Matching hero VT name; back Link types; Suspense VT enter/exit; optional page VT wrapper |
| `/workspace/app/page.tsx` | Optional Suspense VT wrappers around grid/skeleton |
| `/workspace/app/ProductSkeleton.tsx` | Usually unchanged (wrapped by parent VT) |
| `/workspace/app/globals.css` | morph, nav-forward/back, slide-up/down, fade, reduced-motion |
| `/workspace/app/layout.tsx` | Optional: sticky header with `viewTransitionName: 'site-header'` if you add chrome |
| `/workspace/lib/products.ts` | Unchanged (unless you add real image URLs later) |

---

## Architecture notes for implementers

1. **Everything is a Server Component today** — `ViewTransition` and `Link` work in RSC; no `'use client'` required for the guide patterns.
2. **“Images” are color blocks** — morph still works on any DOM element pair with the same `name`.
3. **Only real async delay** is the 100ms in `ProductDetails` — that is what exercises Suspense reveal on detail.
4. **`ProductGrid` is sync** — home Suspense fallback may never flash in production without adding delay or making the grid async.
5. **No extra npm packages** — use React’s `<ViewTransition>` + Next’s `experimental.viewTransition` + CSS `::view-transition-*`.
6. **Authoritative reference** in this install:  
   `/workspace/node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/view-transitions.md`  
   (same four patterns: shared morph, Suspense reveal, directional nav, same-route crossfade).

